---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { Text, Tooltip } from '@antadesign/anta'
import { StickerThumbsUpAnimated } from '@antadesign/stickers'
---

<DocsLayout title="Overview">
  <h1>Overview</h1>

  <div class="overview-intro">
    <div class="overview-sticker">
      <StickerThumbsUpAnimated size={256} />
    </div>
    <div class="overview-copy">
      <Text size="large">
        <p>The <a href="https://antithesis.com" target="_blank">Antithesis</a> design system, <b>Anta</b>, is pretty cool because:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>it's carefully made <dfn>for web apps<Tooltip follow>Import the whole library (~100kb gzipped)<br />or selected components to minimize your bundle.<br />There is <b>no CSS-in-JS runtime</b>.</Tooltip></dfn></li>
          <li>has a <dfn>clean, attribute-driven DOM<Tooltip follow><b>No piles of utility classes and wrapping containers</b>.<br />Variants, tones, and behavior are attributes: <code>tone="critical"</code>, <code>size="large"</code>.</Tooltip></dfn></li>
          <li>is <dfn>easy to override<Tooltip follow>Global CSS tokens (auto-switching default light/dark styles) with <b>an optional theme</b>.<br />Customizable with attributes or plain CSS at the per-component level.</Tooltip></dfn></li>
          <li>has framework-agnostic <dfn>web components<Tooltip follow>The web components are fully declarative: they never change their own attributes<br />(an Antithesis architecture requirement related to worker-thread UI rendering).</Tooltip></dfn></li>
          <li>uses <dfn>JSX wrappers<Tooltip follow>For dynamic state and conditional composition.</Tooltip></dfn> for <dfn>React or Preact<Tooltip>React is a default runtime.<br />Preact works via compat.<br />Use custom runtime via <code>configure()</code>.</Tooltip></dfn></li>
          <li>it's well documented, typed, and AI-ready</li>
        </ul>
      </Text>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .overview-intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .overview-sticker { flex: none; }
  .overview-copy { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }

  /* Stack on narrow screens — sticker first (it leads the source order). */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .overview-intro { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>
